# Build output
/build/
build/
cmake-build-*/

# .NET
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user

# Local managed publish placed next to the extension. The in-build output is
# already covered by /build/ above; this guards any publish placed elsewhere.
# Do NOT ignore the C++ core SOURCE, which lives under src/arrownet/.
**/arrownet/
!src/arrownet/
!src/include/arrownet/

# Python scaffold leftovers (uv) — superseded by the C++/C# project
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.venv/

# mssql-extension compatibility corpus — generated from the sibling mssql-extension
# repo by scripts/gen_mssqlcompat_tests.sh (not committed; regenerate on demand).
/test/mssqlcompat/

# Editor / tooling (machine-local)
.vscode/
.serena/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local credentials / connection recipes — contain live secrets, never commit.
/fabric.md
/adls_account.txt
/adls_secret.sql

# dbt-duckdb harnesses — the SOURCE (dbt_project.yml, models/, macros/, plugins/, seeds/,
# snapshots/, pyproject.toml, uv.lock, profiles.example.yml) is tracked; SECRETS + generated
# state are NOT. profiles.yml holds live connstrs/SP secrets → never commit (use the .example).
dbt_mssql_test/profiles.yml
dbt_dax_test/profiles.yml
dbt_*/.venv/
dbt_*/target/
dbt_*/logs/
dbt_*/dbt_packages/
dbt_*/**/__pycache__/

# DuckDB database state — generated, and can persist secrets (CREATE SECRET / attach connstrs);
# never commit anywhere.
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
fabric-test.local.env
dax_secret.sql

# Scratch/temporary working files (spikes, ad-hoc SQL, throwaway test dirs).
/scratchpad/

# test-only TLS material generated by docker/certs/generate-certs.ps1
docker/certs/*.crt
docker/certs/*.key
docker/certs/openssl.cnf

# Fabricator debug logs (FABRICATOR_LOG_FILE)
*.fablog

# Agent project memory — local only (user decision, 2026-08-11). It is dense internal working notes rather
# than anything a reader of this repo wants, so it is kept OUT of the published tree.
#
# ⚠ ANCHORED (leading slash) ON PURPOSE: an unanchored `CLAUDE.md` would also ignore one in any subdirectory,
# and per-directory agent memory is a thing this repo may want to track later.
#
# ⚠ IT WAS TRACKED UNTIL NOW, so ignoring alone would have done nothing — it was untracked with
# `git rm --cached CLAUDE.md`, which stages its removal. Two consequences worth knowing:
#   * the file is NOT removed from HISTORY — every earlier commit still shows it;
#   * it no longer syncs between machines, which is what its own header said keeping it in the repo was for.
#     Anyone working on a second checkout needs to bring it across by hand.
# `scripts/check-docs.sh` already guards its two CLAUDE.md reads with os.path.exists, so a clone without it
# still passes rather than failing on a missing file.
/CLAUDE.md
